INT. APPELLATE COURTROOM - DAY

Dark wood, high bench, a brass seal. A hush. ATTORNEY RUTH ELLINGSWORTH, 50s, stands at the lectern in a navy suit. Her papers are squared. Her hands are not.

JUSTICE AMADOU DIALLO-FERNANDEZ, 60s, looks down from the bench over half-moon glasses. He has been listening for an hour.

JUSTICE DIALLO-FERNANDEZ
Ms. Ellingsworth, your time is nearly up.

RUTH
I understand, Your Honor. If I may conclude.

JUSTICE DIALLO-FERNANDEZ
You may.

RUTH
The trial court erred in excluding the recording. Without it, the jury never heard my client's own words.

JUSTICE DIALLO-FERNANDEZ
Words he spoke to a priest.

RUTH
To a man who was not, in fact, a priest.

JUSTICE DIALLO-FERNANDEZ
So you say.

RUTH
So the record says. Exhibit nine.

He flips pages. She waits. The door at the back opens with a creak. A BAILIFF, 30s, hurries down the aisle and hands the Justice a folded note. He reads. His face changes.

JUSTICE DIALLO-FERNANDEZ (CONT'D)
Ms. Ellingsworth, I'm informed that the State has just withdrawn its opposition.

RUTH
Withdrawn?

JUSTICE DIALLO-FERNANDEZ
Entirely. Your client's conviction is to be vacated.

Ruth looks at the back of the room. Her opponent's chair is empty. Her phone buzzes against the lectern. She turns it over. A name on the screen.

RUTH
Your Honor, may I take this?

JUSTICE DIALLO-FERNANDEZ
Please.

She raises the phone to her ear.

BAILIFF (V.O.)
(over phone)
Ma'am, front desk. The real priest just walked in. He confirmed it.

Ruth lowers the phone and lets her breath out slowly. The Justice watches her. She nods once.

RUTH
Thank you, Your Honor.

JUSTICE DIALLO-FERNANDEZ
Don't thank me yet. The paperwork alone will take until Friday.

RUTH
Friday is fine.

JUSTICE DIALLO-FERNANDEZ
I thought it might be.

She gathers her papers. He returns to his notes without another glance. The Bailiff holds the door. Ruth walks out with a straight back and unsteady knees.

INT. COURTHOUSE CORRIDOR - CONTINUOUS

Marble floors. Echoes. She leans against a column and closes her eyes. The Bailiff appears at her shoulder.

BAILIFF
Ma'am, you dropped this.

He hands her a single sheet. Exhibit nine. She folds it into her coat.

RUTH
He's going to walk out of there tonight.

BAILIFF
Yes, ma'am.

RUTH
Eleven years.

The Bailiff says nothing. He just nods. She smiles, finally, and goes.
